Z||000004||Dave Gunsul||10-14-2001||02:23 AM||||Yes the Fiero store does sponser shows and sends door prizes all the time. Two shows that i can think of off the top of my head are: the Dells Run (WI Fiero Fanatics) and<BR>N.I.F.E.'s Fierorama. They also give NIFE members a 10% discount. <P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||14
Z||000005||Master_Sushi||10-14-2001||11:06 AM||||I've heard they also do other cars besides fieros. Something like MGs or something. Its been a while since I heard this so im not sure where I heard it from  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. I've ordered from the fiero store and had no probs at all. I think they are great!||||reg||14
Z||000006||Fformula88||10-14-2001||11:28 AM||||I know of no show cars from there or employees on here.<P>Everyone says that they give 10% to any Fiero club member, even if its just PFF.  You just have to tell them when you call.  Also, its not available on GM parts.  <P>Despite the recent problems between Rodney and FS, I will still buy from them based on the great service I have gotten from them in the past.  I would also buy from Rodney without question.  I've seen his stuff at Fiero events and it all looks great!  I think the FS will become very important to the Fiero community in the future, and want to help keep them around.  They are one of the few places out there supporting the Fiero cummunity by keeping basic parts available (brake parts, esp for 88's.  Try getting it at Napa-its either not available or 3X the price!!).  I know people have had problems with some of their custom stuff, but as GM and regular parts stores stop carrying things, its nice to have a source to get stuff.  ||||reg||1
